
@1=~Welcome among the dead, Blood of Bhaal.~
@2=~Who are you?~ 
@3=~Caris, I was the master's personal embalmer.~
@4=~In this place, I make sure to find a place for each of our guests. However, there are four chests on this level reserved for the dead. Find the four keys, and the chests will open to reveal a special item. Placed correctly in the four niches, these items will open a gateway to another death. In my opinion, much less pleasant than this one. I assure you, none of our clients have complained so far! (big smile)~
@5=~Welcome among the dead, servant of the Blood of Bhaal.~
@6=~Who are you?~ 
@7=~Caris, I was the master's personal embalmer.~
@9=~I see with regret that the fire coffins did not please you. Some prefer to remain on the bare ground. Personally, I think it's important to be comfortable in one's eternal demise.~ 
@10=~Urglite's coffins didn't catch your eye. A little too icy perhaps?~
@11=~Don't worry, you'll find yours. We still have plenty of coffins to offer you.~
@12=~You have a strange sense of humor...~
@15=~I'm quite serious. Murder is handled with the utmost care.~
@16=~Be a little patient, we'll find you a fine murder, with blood and pain.~ 
@18=~Well, I note with great pleasure that we are dealing with fine guests. Your murder hasn't found you yet.~
@24=~Your departure saddens me; we haven't found the death that suits you... There are few we haven't been able to satisfy. Arm yourself with wisdom; you will need it for your next trial.~ 
@25=~It was a real pleasure to see you toying with murder. (The effigy closes its eyes, a smile on its lips)~
@26=~(No response)~ 
@27=~Caris's Info: Caris, Bhaal's embalmer, informs me that to proceed to the next trial, I must place four objects in niches. The catch is that I must find the four chests and keys to locate the objects. Then I must place them correctly in the niches...~
